Audio headroom: the mix is lowered by about 3 dB before the limiter, so it only
catches rare spikes (it was turning loud battles down 15% of the time), and the
limiter lets go over 0.35 s instead of 0.15 s, so it pumps less.
<prefix>_AUDIO_FULL_LEVEL keeps the old level. (2026-11-24)

--- a/host/audio/audio_sink.cpp
+++ b/host/audio/audio_sink.cpp
@@ -47,7 +47,17 @@
 constexpr double kKnee = 29500.0;
 constexpr std::size_t kLookahead = 64u;  // ~1.5 ms
 constexpr double kAttackFrames = 16.0;
-constexpr double kReleaseSeconds = 0.15;
+constexpr double kReleaseSeconds = 0.35;  // 0.15 until 2026-11-24: let go slower, less pumping
+
+// Headroom (2026-11-24, owner on good headphones): the whole mix is lowered by
+// about 3 dB before the limiter, so it only catches the rare spike. Before,
+// loud VC2 battles had the limiter turning sound down in 39 of 143 seconds
+// (15% of all frames), which squashes and pumps. <prefix>_AUDIO_FULL_LEVEL
+// keeps the old level.
+[[nodiscard]] double headroom() {
+    static const double gain = portablekit::env("AUDIO_FULL_LEVEL") != nullptr ? 1.0 : 0.70795;  // -3 dB
+    return gain;
+}
 
